nance":{"locator":"editorial-projection artifact physical lines 83-85; antecedent 1922 Tours Mame, printed p. 935; artifact PDF p. 1049; text-layer lines 50-58 of that page","provenance_authority":"Triptych editorial projection verified by page-image collation against the 1962 target edition","provenance_confidence":"high","provenance_evidence":"The project-owned projection passage reproduces the retained calendar body hash exactly. Its artifact manifest records the bounded public-domain 1862 Pustet antecedent, the separate 1962 target, and every editorial transformation; neither witness is represented as owning the projected bytes. The 1962 reading was established on that edition's page images rather than its text layer, cross-read against the Benziger conformed printing. Differences from the antecedent: token 0: 1962 prints \"Maiestati tuae,\"; 1922 Tours Mame reads \"pean tuz,\" (edit distance 8); token 6: 1962 prints \"quaesumus:\"; 1922 Tours Mame reads \"quzsumus :\" (edit distance 2); token 16: 1962 prints \"beatae\"; 1922 Tours Mame reads \"beatze\" (edit distance 1); token 22: 1962 prints \"eundem\"; 1922 Tours Mame reads \"eumdem\" (edit distance 1, conclusion); token 24: 1962 prints \"nostrum.\"; 1922 Tours Mame reads \"Przfatio\" (edit distance 6, conclusion); 1922 Mame prints Majestati where the 1962 prints Maiestati; 1922 Mame sets a semicolon after accendat where the 1962 sets a comma; 1922 Mame ends Per eumdem Dominum., the 1962 Per eundem Dominum nostrum.. Corroboration: 1862 Pustet Ratisbon text-layer lines 96784-96791: 14 of 25 tokens identical after normalisation (n-gram similarity 0.60); 1604 Vatican typical: swept end to end, no matching text (best window n-gram similarity 0.14, which is noise).","relationship":"editorial-projection-exact-to-target","source_date":"2026-09-03 project editorial projection; antecedent Pustet Ratisbon 1862","source_id":"passage.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-09-03.immaculati-cordis-beatae-mariae-virginis-secret","status":"collated","transformations":["join printed line wraps","remove stress accents","expand printed ae/oe ligatures to ae/oe","normalise consonantal i to the calendar's j orthography","apply the target printing's punctuation","carry the target's conclusion at its printed length"],"verification_locator":"printed p. 634, no. 3433; artifact PDF p. 715","verification_source_id":"passage.catholic-church.missale-romanum.vatican-typica-1962.temporal-immaculati-cordis-beatae-mariae-virginis-orations"},"publication":{"basis":"public-domain","evidence":"The wording is preexisting material of the 1962 typical edition under 17 U.S.C. 103(b), which gives a revised edition no exclusive right in material it did not contribute. The independent registered public-domain witness is the tracked 1862 Pustet text artifact. The position is settled for the repository at src/sources/inventories/missale-romanum-1962-facsimile-rights-v1.toml, which names the seasonal orations as preexisting material and requires exactly this pairing of 103(b) with a public-domain witness.","locator":"Pustet Ratisbon 1862, 1922 Tours Mame, printed p. 935; artifact PDF p. 1049; text-layer lines 50-58 of that page; artifact rights_status public-domain","source_ids":["artifact.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-09-03.gap-marian-orations-94a91c93","artifact.catholic-church.missale-romanum.pustet-ratisbon-1862.missale-romanum-1862-text-f34bc7cf"],"status":"permitted","surfaces":["cli","corpus-data","download","print","public-git","web"]},"reason":null,"text_sha256":"7f5b044d27f4c84141bb492ef88677e94c98dd3e279f4cdba95fd58615a032eb","withheld":false},"name":"Secret","source":"composed","taken_from":null,"text":"Majestati tuae, Domine, Agnum immaculatum offerentes, quaesumus: ut corda\nnostra ignis ille divinus accendat, qui Cor beatae Mariae Virginis\nineffabiliter inflammavit. Per eundem Dominum nostrum.\n","text_status":null,"translations":[{"caution":"Original study translation; not approved for liturgical use or recitation.","lang":"en","rights":"project-created","source_label":"Triptych study English","text":"As we offer the immaculate Lamb to your majesty, Lord, we ask that the divine fire that ineffably inflamed the Heart of the Blessed Virgin Mary may kindle our hearts. Through the same Lord of ours.\n"}],"unavailable_translations":null,"untranslated":null},{"citations":[{"book":"John","loci":{"hebrew":[{"chapter":19,"first":26,"last":27}],"hebrew-unnumbered-titles":[{"chapter":19,"first":26,"last":27}],"vulgate":[{"chapter":19,"first":26,"last":27}]},"ref":"John 19:26-27","token":"John","unresolved":null}],"coverage":{"component":"scripture","cycle":"all","cycle_family":null,"languages":[{"availability":"unresolved","collation":"unresolved","lang":"la","publication_basis":"unresolved","relationship":"bible-reconstruction","witnesses":[]},{"availability":"unresolved","collation":"unresolved","lang":"en","publication_basis":"unresolved","relationship":"bible-reconstruction","witnesses":[]}],"occurrence_id":"roman-1962%3Aimmaculati-cordis-beatae-mariae-virginis%3Amain%3A9:all:all","schema":"triptych-missal-unit-coverage/v1","target_id":"roman-1962%3Aproper%3Aimmaculati-cordis-beatae-mariae-virginis%3Amain%3ACommunion%3A1:all:all"},"cycles":{},"form":"","form_id":"main","incipit":null,"languages":[{"available":false,"held":false,"lang":"la","reason":"delegated-to-scripture","status":"scripture-delegated"},{"available":false,"held":false,"lang":"en","reason":"delegated-to-scripture","status":"scripture-delegated"}],"latin":null,"name":"Communion","source":"scripture","taken_from":null,"text":null,"text_status":null,"translations":null,"unavailable_translations":null,"untranslated":null},{"citations":[],"coverage":{"component":"proper-body","cycle":"all","cycle_family":null,"languages":[{"availability":"available","collation":"collated","lang":"la","publication_basis":"qualified-