posed","taken_from":null,"text":"Divinis refecti muneribus te, Domine, suppliciter exoramus: ut beatae Mariae Virginis intercessione, cujus immaculati Cordis solemnia (memoriam) venerando egimus, a praesentibus periculis liberati, aeternae vitae gaudia consequamur. Per Dominum.\n","text_status":null,"translations":[{"caution":"Original study translation; not approved for liturgical use or recitation.","lang":"en","rights":"project-created","source_label":"Triptych study English","text":"Nourished by divine gifts, Lord, we humbly ask you that, through the intercession of the Blessed Virgin Mary, whose Immaculate Heart we have reverently honored with this solemn celebration (commemoration), we may be freed from present dangers and attain the joys of eternal life. Through the Lord."}],"unavailable_translations":null,"untranslated":null}],"registry":"1962-08-22","season":null,"takes_from":null,"text_status":null},"schema":"triptych-propers-read-mass/v1"}
